      {
        "id": "blk-h-insights",
        "type": "heading",
        "data": { "level": 2, "text": "Key insights" }
      },
      {
        "id": "blk-insights",
        "type": "text",
        "data": {
          "markdown": "- **Consistent upward trend:** a 7-point rise between January and March in the satisfaction score.\n- **Regional gap:** coastal metros at 85+, while the Mountain region sits in the 78-79 range.\n- **Strength:** **ease of use** is the top-rated dimension (77% *agree* or *strongly agree*).\n- **Area to improve:** **value for money** — only 54% rated it *agree* or above.\n- **Support availability** still shows high variance. Worth examining coverage across time zones."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "blk-h-recs",
        "type": "heading",
        "data": { "level": 2, "text": "Recommendations" }
      },
      {
        "id": "blk-recs",
        "type": "text",
        "data": {
          "markdown": "1. Launch a regional pilot in the Mountain region — tailored onboarding and tighter support SLAs.\n2. Revisit the US pricing structure, especially for new customers (<6 months).\n3. Repeat the survey in Q2 with the same methodology to measure the impact of the interventions.\n4. Run 20-30 qualitative interviews with respondents who scored ≤5 to understand drivers of low satisfaction."
        }
